            "bug_id": 18639,
            "text": "Please export `tools:::.split_dependencies()`. It's important for any author trying to parse DESCRIPTION files correctly, which has any number of use cases for writing tooling. I've hand-written similar logic dozens of times in subtly incorrect ways, as have other authors. I very quickly find 100 examples in CRAN packages:\n\nhttps://github.com/search?q=org%3Acran+%2Fread%5B.%5Ddcf%5B%28%5D%2F+%2F%5B%27%22%5DDESCRIPTION%2F+%2Fstrsplit%5B%28%5D%2F&type=code\n\nThe function is very stable (I don't see any substantive change in 15 years). Is there any reason to keep it private? It seems like having a canonical mapping from plaintext-in-DESCRIPTION to a corresponding parsed data structure is a good tool to share.",
            "creation_time": "2023-12-19T01:17:56Z"
          }
        ]
